{"name":"Laviguer","status":"ok","title":"Laviguer","pageId":64845,"html":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" dir=\"ltr\" lang=\"en\"><p class=\"mw-empty-elt\">\n</p><aside class=\"portable-infobox pi-background pi-border-color pi-theme-frwiki pi-layout-default type-location\" role=\"region\">\n\n<nav class=\"pi-navigation pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-font\"><a href=\"/wiki/Category:Maps_of_Laviguer\" title=\"Category:Maps of Laviguer\">Gallery</a></nav>\n<h2 class=\"pi-item pi-item-spacing pi-title pi-secondary-background\" data-source=\"name\">Laviguer</h2>\n<section class=\"pi-item pi-group pi-border-color\">\n<h2 class=\"pi-item pi-header pi-secondary-font pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-background\">Geography</h2>\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"type\">\n<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Type</h3>\n<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\">Town</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"region\">\n<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Region</h3>\n<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\"><a href=\"/wiki/Impiltur\" title=\"Impiltur\">Impiltur</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Northeast_Faer%C3%BBn\" title=\"Northeast Faerûn\">northeast Faerûn</a></div>\n</div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"pi-item pi-group pi-border-color\">\n<h2 class=\"pi-item pi-header pi-secondary-font pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-background\">Society</h2>\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"races\">\n<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Races</h3>\n<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\"><a href=\"/wiki/Human\" title=\"Human\">Humans</a></div>\n</div>\n</section>\n<h2 class=\"pi-item pi-header pi-secondary-font pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-background\">History<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-tBSL-p15_1-0\"><a href=\"#cite_note-tBSL-p15-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup><sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-CoV-p125_2-0\"><a href=\"#cite_note-CoV-p125-2\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>2<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></h2>\n<section class=\"pi-item pi-group pi-border-color\">\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"ruler1\">\n<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Ruler</h3>\n<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\"><a href=\"/wiki/Haelimbrar\" title=\"Haelimbrar\">Haelimbrar</a> in <a href=\"/wiki/1357_DR\" title=\"1357 DR\">1357 DR</a><br/>Haelimbrar in <a href=\"/wiki/1374_DR\" title=\"1374 DR\">1374 DR</a></div>\n</div>\n</section>\n<nav class=\"pi-navigation pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-font\"><a class=\"newcategory\" href=\"/wiki/Category:Inhabitants_of_Laviguer\" title=\"Category:Inhabitants of Laviguer\">Inhabitants of  Laviguer</a></nav>\n<nav class=\"pi-navigation pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-font\"><span class=\"new\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvQ2F0ZWdvcnk6T3JnYW5pemF0aW9uc19pbl9MYXZpZ3Vlcj9hY3Rpb249ZWRpdCZyZWRsaW5rPTE=\" title=\"Category:Organizations in Laviguer (page does not exist)\">Organizations in  Laviguer</span></nav>\n</aside>\n<p class=\"mw-empty-elt\"></p><p><b>Laviguer</b> was a mining town in the kingdom of <a href=\"/wiki/Impiltur\" title=\"Impiltur\">Impiltur</a> in <a href=\"/wiki/Northeast_Faer%C3%BBn\" title=\"Northeast Faerûn\">northeast Faerûn</a>.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Impiltur_3-0\"><a href=\"#cite_note-Impiltur-3\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>3<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<div aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\" class=\"toc\" id=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\"><input class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" role=\"button\" style=\"display:none\" type=\"checkbox\"/><div class=\"toctitle\" dir=\"ltr\" lang=\"en\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Geography\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Geography</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Description\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Description</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#People\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">People</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Government\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Government</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Law_&amp;_Order\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Law &amp; Order</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Notable_inhabitants\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Notable inhabitants</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#References\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">References</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Geography\">Geography</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a aria-label=\"Edit section: Geography\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-action=\"edit-section\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Laviguer?veaction=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Geography\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>It lay in the Uplands of northwestern Impiltur, at the foot of the <a href=\"/wiki/Earthspur_Mountains\" title=\"Earthspur Mountains\">Earthspur Mountains</a>, at the end of the <span class=\"new\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvUHJpbmNlJTI3c19Sb2FkP2FjdGlvbj1lZGl0JnJlZGxpbms9MQ==\" title=\"Prince's Road (page does not exist)\">Prince's Road</span>.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Impiltur_3-1\"><a href=\"#cite_note-Impiltur-3\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>3<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Description\">Description</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a aria-label=\"Edit section: Description\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-action=\"edit-section\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Laviguer?veaction=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Description\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Laviguer was a hub for the mining industry in the Earthspur Mountains, working in competition with the neighboring town of <a href=\"/wiki/Vordric_Dun\" title=\"Vordric Dun\">Vordric Dun</a>. The mining trade here was very profitable for the kingdom. However, they were rough and rowdy places.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Impiltur_3-2\"><a href=\"#cite_note-Impiltur-3\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>3<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"People\">People</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a aria-label=\"Edit section: People\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-action=\"edit-section\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Laviguer?veaction=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: People\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Laviguer was full of hard-working, hard-living, and hard-drinking men and women who worked the mines.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Impiltur_3-3\"><a href=\"#cite_note-Impiltur-3\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>3<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Government\">Government</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a aria-label=\"Edit section: Government\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-action=\"edit-section\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Laviguer?veaction=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Government\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>War-Captain <a href=\"/wiki/Haelimbrar\" title=\"Haelimbrar\">Haelimbrar</a>, one of the <a href=\"/wiki/Lords_of_Imphras_II\" title=\"Lords of Imphras II\">Lords of Imphras II</a>, was based in Laviguer. He was charged with securing the northern and western borders of the realm, but was often away on secret missions.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-tBSL-p15_1-1\"><a href=\"#cite_note-tBSL-p15-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup><sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-CoV-p125_2-1\"><a href=\"#cite_note-CoV-p125-2\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>2<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Law_.26_Order\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Law_&amp;_Order\">Law &amp; Order</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a aria-label=\"Edit section: Law &amp; Order\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-action=\"edit-section\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Laviguer?veaction=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Law &amp; Order\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The <span class=\"new\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvV2Fyc3dvcmRzX29mX0ltcGlsdHVyP2FjdGlvbj1lZGl0JnJlZGxpbms9MQ==\" title=\"Warswords of Impiltur (page does not exist)\">Warswords of Impiltur</span>, and through them the Council of Lords, policed Laviguer heavily, with crackdowns on criminal activity and regularly placing it under \"daggerbond\", a martial law that forbade the open wearing of weapons within the town. They were flexible with the miners, though, owing to the riches they brought to the realm.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Impiltur_3-4\"><a href=\"#cite_note-Impiltur-3\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>3<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Notable_inhabitants\">Notable inhabitants</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a aria-label=\"Edit section: Notable inhabitants\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-action=\"edit-section\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Laviguer?veaction=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Notable inhabitants\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Around <a href=\"/wiki/1374_DR\" title=\"1374 DR\">1374 DR</a>, one \"Sarshel of Laviguer\" was in fact the young King <a href=\"/wiki/Imbrar_II\" title=\"Imbrar II\">Imbrar II</a> living in deep cover to avoid assassins prior to his coronation,<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-CoV-p92_4-0\"><a href=\"#cite_note-CoV-p92-4\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>4<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup> under the protection of the <a href=\"/wiki/Order_of_the_Bladewright\" title=\"Order of the Bladewright\">Order of the Bladewright</a>.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-CC-PC_5-0\"><a href=\"#cite_note-CC-PC-5\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>5<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"References\">References</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a aria-label=\"Edit section: References\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-action=\"edit-section\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Laviguer?veaction=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: References\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<div class=\"reflist\" style=\"\">\n<div class=\"mw-references-wrap\"><ol class=\"references\">\n<li id=\"cite_note-tBSL-p15-1\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\">↑ <sup><a href=\"#cite_ref-tBSL-p15_1-0\">1.0</a></sup> <sup><a href=\"#cite_ref-tBSL-p15_1-1\">1.1</a></sup></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><a href=\"/wiki/R.A._Salvatore\" title=\"R.A. Salvatore\">R.A. Salvatore</a> (1989). <i><a href=\"/wiki/The_Bloodstone_Lands_(sourcebook)\" title=\"The Bloodstone Lands (sourcebook)\">The Bloodstone Lands</a></i>. Edited by <a href=\"/wiki/Elizabeth_T._Danforth\" title=\"Elizabeth T. Danforth\">Elizabeth T. Danforth</a>. (<a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/wiki/TSR,_Inc\" title=\"TSR, Inc\">TSR, Inc</a>), p. 15. ISBN <a href=\"/wiki/Special:BookSources/0-88038-771-8\" title=\"Special:BookSources/0-88038-771-8\">0-88038-771-8</a>.</span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite_note-CoV-p125-2\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\">↑ <sup><a href=\"#cite_ref-CoV-p125_2-0\">2.0</a></sup> <sup><a href=\"#cite_ref-CoV-p125_2-1\">2.1</a></sup></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><a href=\"/wiki/Thomas_M._Reid\" title=\"Thomas M. Reid\">Thomas M. Reid</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Sean_K._Reynolds\" title=\"Sean K. Reynolds\">Sean K. Reynolds</a> (Nov. 2005). <i><a href=\"/wiki/Champions_of_Valor\" title=\"Champions of Valor\">Champions of Valor</a></i>. (<a href=\"/wiki/Wizards_of_the_Coast\" title=\"Wizards of the Coast\">Wizards of the Coast</a>), p. 125. ISBN <a href=\"/wiki/Special:BookSources/0-7869-3697-5\" title=\"Special:BookSources/0-7869-3697-5\">0-7869-3697-5</a>.</span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite_note-Impiltur-3\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\">↑ <sup><a href=\"#cite_ref-Impiltur_3-0\">3.0</a></sup> <sup><a href=\"#cite_ref-Impiltur_3-1\">3.1</a></sup> <sup><a href=\"#cite_ref-Impiltur_3-2\">3.2</a></sup> <sup><a href=\"#cite_ref-Impiltur_3-3\">3.3</a></sup> <sup><a href=\"#cite_ref-Impiltur_3-4\">3.4</a></sup></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><a href=\"/wiki/George_Krashos\" title=\"George Krashos\">George Krashos</a> (August 2006). “Impiltur: The Forgotten Kingdom”. In <